-- title:
--   Semilinear transport of smooth-point packages, q=3
-- statement:
--   Frame and data. Fixed are a prime $q$ together with the hypothesis $q=3$, a natural number $M'$ with $M'\neq 0$ and $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$; write $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ is given together with the hypothesis `hW` that membership in $W$ is equivalent to membership in `ssPlaces q M' κ`, i.e. to being a place $w$ that is rational, satisfies the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and has `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')` in `ssJSet q κ`; an element $s\in W$ is fixed. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of intermediate fields of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, the source being the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field and the target the base change of the $X_H$-function field for $q^2M'$ and the subgroup `levelH q M'`. Finally, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with reduction field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` lying over $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which is compatible with the residue map of $A$, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of functions, and the clause that every non-zero element acquires a non-zero residue after multiplication by a suitable constant), and `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   The prolongation and the package data. $FSS$ is a field over $\kappa$, and $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with reduction field $FSS$: a valuation subring `R.integers` of `fieldBar q M'` whose intersection with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism `R.residue` onto $FSS$ with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with the residue map of $A$, and the scaling clause for non-zero elements. Moreover $N$ is a finite set of places of $FSS$ over $\kappa$, and for every place $Q$ of $FSS$ over $\kappa$ there are given a subring $S_Q=$ `Sx Q` of `fieldBar q M'`, a ring homomorphism $\varphi_Q:A[T]\to S_Q$, a ring homomorphism $\chi_{0,Q}:S_Q\to\kappa$, and a set $D_Q=$ `Dx Q` of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   Hypotheses on these data. `h0`: $FSS$ contains an element transcendental over $\kappa$. `h1` (the link with $s$): for every $f\in$ `R₀.integers` such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the base change of `jq` has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` lies in `R.integers` and its $R$-residue is the image under `algebraMap κ FSS` of `s.evalAt` of the $R_0$-residue of $f$. `h2`: for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, the preimage of `R.integers` under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is `R.integers`. `hcard`: $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   `hpkg` (thirteen clauses, summarised here) requires, for every place $Q\notin N$, that $(S_Q,\varphi_Q,\chi_{0,Q},D_Q)$ be a smooth-point package: $S_Q$ contains the image of $A$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_Q$ composed with `Polynomial.C` is the structure map of $A$, and $\chi_{0,Q}$ composed with it is the residue map of $A$; $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(T))=0$; for each $c\in A$ with residue $0$ there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi:S_Q\to A$ restricting to the identity on the image of $A$, reducing to $\chi_{0,Q}$, and sending $\varphi_Q(T)$ to $c$; every $f\in S_Q$ lies in `R.integers`, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there is the image of $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$ in the residue field of $Q$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q(T)$ has $Q$-order $1$; $D_Q$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ such that every $f\in S_Q$ is $P$-integral with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$, and such that $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $<1$ precisely when $\chi_{0,Q}(f)=0$; each section $\chi:S_Q\to A$ as above arises from a unique $P\in D_Q$ via $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$; for $P\in D_Q$ the valuation subring of $P$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in S_Q$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(h)\neq 0$; every non-zero $f$ of order $0$ at all $P\in D_Q$ becomes, after multiplication by the image of a non-zero constant, a unit of $S_Q$; and every $f\in$ `R.integers` integral at all $P\in D_Q$ lies in $S_Q$.
--
--   `hdisj`: for $Q,Q'\notin N$ the discs $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$ are disjoint unless $Q=Q'$. `hcusp` (cusp-freeness): for $Q\notin N$ and $P\in D_Q$, the order at $P$ of the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the base change of `jq` is non-negative. `heqv` (equivariance): for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves `R.integers`, the induced automorphism `R.resAut τ` of $FSS$ satisfies: $\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q\in N$ if and only if $Q\in N$, and for $Q\notin N$ one has `smulDisc τ (Dx Q) = Dx (R.resAut τ _ • Q)`, where `smulDisc τ D = {P | τ⁻¹ • P ∈ D}`.
--
--   `hNpkg` (no package at the $q+1$ ends): for every $Q\in N$ and all data $(S,\varphi,\chi_0,D)$ of the same shape, the conjunction of the thirteen package clauses above together with the cusp-freeness clause for $D$ fails. `hUniq` (uniqueness off $N$): for every $Q\notin N$, any data $(S,\varphi,\chi_0,D)$ satisfying the thirteen package clauses satisfy $D=D_Q$ as sets of places, $S=S_Q$ as subsets of `fieldBar q M'`, and $\chi_0$ agrees with $\chi_{0,Q}$ on common elements.
--
--   Conclusion. Under these hypotheses, the following holds for every semilinear automorphism $g$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an element of `SemilinearAut`, that is a pair consisting of a ring automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` and a ring automorphism `SemilinearAut.baseAut g` of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ intertwined by the structure map), subject to: `hgA`, that `baseAut g` preserves $A$ in the sense that $\mathrm{baseAut}(g)(x)\in A$ iff $x\in A$; `hgR`, that $g\cdot f\in$ `R.integers` iff $f\in$ `R.integers`; `hgj`, that $g$ fixes the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the base change of `jq`; together with a ring automorphism $\psi$ of $\kappa$ satisfying `hψ`, that $\psi$ of the residue of $a\in A$ is the residue of $\mathrm{baseAut}(g)(a)$, and a ring automorphism $\phi$ of $FSS$ satisfying `hφ`, that $R.\mathrm{residue}(g\cdot f)=\phi(R.\mathrm{residue}(f))$ for all $f\in$ `R.integers`. For all places $Q,Q'$ of $FSS$ over $\kappa$ with $Q\notin N$ and such that $y$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q'$ exactly when $\phi^{-1}(y)$ lies in that of $Q$, one then has: $Q'\notin N$; and there is a proof $h_S$ that $f\in S_Q$ if and only if $g\cdot f\in S_{Q'}$, for which, first, $\chi_{0,Q'}(g\cdot f)=\psi(\chi_{0,Q}(f))$ for every $f\in S_Q$, and second, for every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $P\in D_Q$ if and only if $g\cdot P\in D_{Q'}$.
--
--   This is the functoriality (semilinear transport) statement for the smooth-point data — local subring, residue character and residue disc — attached to the places of the reduction field of a regular prolongation lying over a supersingular place, in the case $q=3$ at an auxiliary level rigidified by a prime $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$. It is used in the assembly of the supersingular component of the stable model, namely by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_nodePresentations_crossUnits_igusaOverS_inertia_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularRegularProlongation_smoothPointCharts_nodePresentations_crossUnits_igusaOverS_inertia_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
